# AdSense and CSP
# Google only documents a nonce strict CSP (script-src with a per-response nonce,
# strict-dynamic, and an https: / http: fallback). Static files cannot mint that nonce.
# strict-dynamic without a nonce would ignore this allowlist and block adsbygoogle.js.
# script-src and connect-src therefore list the Google ad hosts (plus wildcards, because
# the host list changes). script-src also allows 'unsafe-inline' so the official inline
# adsbygoogle.push snippet is not blocked once an ad unit is added.
# frame-src and img-src are https: because there was no frame-src (so frames fell back
# to default-src 'self' and every ad iframe was blocked) and impression images are not
# limited to one host. Ad creatives run in those frames. wasm-unsafe-eval stays for the
# on-page image and GIF tools, including the editor's ONNX Runtime Web session.
# Background removal lazy-loads that runtime from cdn.jsdelivr.net and MODNet from
# Hugging Face (huggingface.co, then the cdn.hf.co host it redirects to).
# object-src, base-uri, frame-ancestors, and form-action stay tight.
